From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 04/05] Canvas anti-fingerprint sub-pixel noise

Perturb the blue channel of getImageData() output so canvas fingerprint
hashes differ from the raw render, defeating CRC/hash-based canvas
fingerprinting while staying visually identical.

QA NOTES (see QA_REPORT.md #04):
  * The doc XORs a FIXED 0x01 on every pixel => the perturbed hash is
    still DETERMINISTIC (same on every render), so it is stable but does
    NOT vary per profile as the checklist claims. To make it vary per
    profile, seed the toggle from a per-session value plumbed in from the
    launcher (e.g. an env-derived seed) instead of a constant.
  * toDataURL()/toBlob() go through getImageData internally in most paths
    but VERIFY on v151; if not, apply the same perturbation in the
    StaticBitmapImage readback path too.
  * API: on v151 confirm the accessor is data()->Data() vs data()->View();
    the buffer accessor name drifts. Adjust before building.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_rendering_context_2d.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/canvas_rendering_context_2d.cc
@@ ImageData* CanvasRenderingContext2D::getImageData(
     ImageData* image_data = BaseRenderingContext2D::getImageData(
         sx, sy, sw, sh, exception_state);
+    if (image_data && image_data->data()) {
+      auto* buffer = image_data->data()->View();
+      uint8_t* pixels = static_cast<uint8_t*>(buffer->BaseAddress());
+      const size_t length = buffer->byteLength();
+      // Sub-pixel perturbation on the blue channel (index i+2), invisible
+      // to the eye but breaks canvas hash fingerprinting.
+      for (size_t i = 0; i + 2 < length; i += 4) {
+        pixels[i + 2] ^= 0x01;
+      }
+    }
     return image_data;
 }
